  "body": "Stacked on #4233. This PR contains the commits of #4233. Merge #4233 first; then this PR takes `git merge origin/main` and a new gate. Do not merge this PR before #4233.\n\n## What changed\n\nThis is slice 2 of #3645: the `.camtools` export and import of tool components and tool stacks.\n\n- `.camtools` version 8 (`ASSEMBLY_VERSION`):\n  - A definition of an assembled tool holds its stack as `assembly`. These are the `project::assembly_wire` links, as a `.camproj` tool states them.\n  - The file holds a top-level `components` array with the rows that the exported stacks name. The rows use the wire form of `project::component_wire` from #4233.\n  - The version step is conditional. A library without a stack keeps its older number (1 to 7) and the same bytes.\n- Strict reading (`crates/app/src/tool_library/assembly.rs`):\n  - The table is read whole. Each row is built again and refused by its id.\n  - Each stack must name rows of the table and resolve, or the file is refused by the tool name.\n  - A row that no stack names is refused by its id.\n  - A file of version 7 or older that states `components` or `assembly` is refused.\n  - The body of an assembled tool goes through `as_derived`, as on a project open (new `project::stack_from_dto`).\n- Import (`crates/app/src/commands/tool_import/`):\n  - `ImportTools` lands the rows and the tools in its one undo step. The table changes first on apply and is restored last on undo.\n  - The rows land in the order of the file table, so an export after the import gives the same bytes.\n  - An added or renamed tool gets its stack. An updated or replaced tool takes the library stack. A library tool without a stack clears the old stack on update, because the record does not come from that stack any more.\n  - \"Holders off\" leaves out the stacks and their rows with the bodies.\n  - `ImportReport` names the added and the reused rows.\n  - The number laws moved to `tool_import/numbers.rs` without a change, to keep `mod.rs` below 400 lines.\n- The id rule (`docs/decisions/3645-camtools-v8.md`). A library row whose id the document already holds:\n  - same content (name, item, geometry): the document row is reused;\n  - different content: the import is refused by the id, and nothing lands.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/app/tests/tool_library_holders/camtools_v8.rs` (a new submodule of the existing `tool_library_holders` suite; no new top-level binary):\n\n- `an_export_of_assembled_tools_is_version_8_and_imports_identically`\n- `a_library_of_plain_tools_keeps_its_older_number_and_imports_as_before`\n- `a_newer_version_and_an_older_file_with_components_are_refused`\n- `a_bad_row_a_bad_link_or_an_unused_row_refuses_the_file_by_name`\n- `undo_and_redo_of_an_import_with_components_restore_tools_and_table`\n- `a_document_row_of_the_same_id_is_reused_when_the_same_and_refuses_when_different`\n\n## Gate results (head `26eab082f`)\n\nThe base of the quick gate is the head of #4233 (`745234df7`). All runs are local, on the Mac.\n\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base 745234df7`), at `323e1430a`: 200 steps, 198 ok, 2 red. The red steps were `holder_reference` and `tool_library`. Their tests named version 8 as the first unknown number. The fix moves them to version 9.\n- The red steps again (`--failed`) on the fix: 2 ok.\n- On the final head `26eab082f` (the only later change is a `type` alias for clippy and the test fix): `app suites: tool_library_holders`, `tool_library`, `holder_reference`, `tool_import_modes`, `tool_table`: all ok. The pinning tests (`gate test camtools_v8`): 6 ok.\n- Strict clippy (`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`) on the final head: clean.\n- Light lane (`cargo xtask gate light`) on the final head: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n- Example catalog suites: not needed. No post and no toolpath changed. They are in the quick plan and were ok.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The MCP reply and the UI import page do not show the component counts yet. The MCP tools are #3647 and the UI is #3648.\n- A stack in the bare `[{name, definition}]` array is refused, because that form has no table.\n\nChangelog: `.camtools` tool libraries now carry tool components and tool assemblies (version 8). The import adds the components in the same undo step, reuses a component of the same content, and refuses a different component of the same id.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: a `.camtools` file with assembled tools is version 8. Builds that read version 7 and older refuse it.\n\nWhat remains on #3645: nothing of the issue text after this PR. This PR merges after #4233, so it closes the issue. The MCP tools (#3647) and the UI (#3648) are separate issues.\n\nFixes #3645\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
